      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Dividing 1 followed by 99 zeros by 7 gives the decimal representation of the number as follows:\n\n$$\\require{cancel}\\frac{1}{7}= 0\\cdots142857\\cdots\\,, \\quad \\text{where the \\dots shows repetition}$$\n\nObserve that the repeating digits have a length of 6.\n\n$$\\longrightarrow 100\\div6=16 \\text{ with a remainder of } 4$$\n\nTherefore, the remainder can indicate the sixth position after the decimal point. In this case, the remainder is 4, therefore the 100th digit after the decimal point is $\\boxed{2}$.\n\n# of digit(s) at the tail end of the decimal representation of 1/7\n\n\n$\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{7}=0.\\overline{142857}\n\\implies 10^{99}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\dots$ \n\nWe just have to find the reminder when we divide $10^{99}$ by 6. Observe that $10\\equiv 4\\pmod{6}\\implies 10^{99} \\equiv 4^{99}\\equiv (\\pm 4)^{50}\\cdot (-4)^{99}\\equiv (-4)^8\\cdot 4^{-99}\\equiv (\\pm 4)^2\\cdot\\frac{-1}{4^6} \\equiv 12\\implies\\boxed{2} $.",
